	{
		"id": "http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/MRS96MCZ",
		"type": "article-journal",
		"abstract": "Abstract\n            Nine characteristics of discontinuous agreement are shown to flow from a syntax that deals in whole phi structures and a linearisation algorithm that renders these discontinuous when conditions converge. This approach is demonstrably superior to reliance solely on syntax, morphology, or the lexicon, outperforming these across a range morphological and syntactic data from Afroasiatic languages and those of Australia and Papua New Guinea.",
		"container-title": "Brill's Journal of Afroasiatic Languages and Linguistics",
		"DOI": "10.1163/18776930-01501009",
		"ISSN": "1876-6633, 1877-6930",
		"issue": "1",
		"note": "The article includes examples from Muher",
		"page": "23-66",
		"source": "DOI.org (Crossref)",
		"title": "Discontinuous Agreement: Nine Birds, Two Stones",
		"URL": "https://brill.com/view/journals/aall/15/1/article-p23_3.xml",
		"volume": "15",
