	{
		"id": "http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/ZHVS2QTD",
		"type": "article-journal",
		"abstract": "The squib focuses on the realization strategies of the final C-slot of templates hosting /j/-final roots in Hebrew and Amharic. Two of these strategies, nonrealization and realization through templatic intrusion, are motivated by the principle *Misalignment. The latter strategy occurs only in nouns, because it employs a suffix marking noncontextual grammatical gender.",
		"container-title": "Linguistic Inquiry",
		"DOI": "10.1162/ling_a_00524",
		"ISSN": "0024-3892, 1530-9150",
		"language": "en",
		"page": "1-15",
		"source": "DOI.org (Crossref)",
		"title": "Intrusion as Template Satisfaction and the QaTaT – QaTa Problem in Semitic",
		"URL": "https://direct.mit.edu/ling/article/doi/10.1162/ling_a_00524/118101/Intrusion-as-Template-Satisfaction-and-the-QaTaT",
		"volume": "not published yet?",
