	{
		"id": "http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/NPGZZ3HI",
		"type": "chapter",
		"abstract": "The mystical Krəstos Ḫarayo – briefly mentioned in the last lines to the medieval hagiographic narration about Saint King Lālibalā, the ‘Life of Lālibalā’ – reappears in an autobiographical note contained in a compilation by a twentieth-century Ethiopian scholar. Critical analysis of this autobiographical note suggests that it was compiled by the modern scholar on the basis of written and oral sources. Consequently, the autobiographical note adds nothing to our knowledge about the actual medieval Ethiopian King Lālibālā’s  court but gives us an insight into twentieth-century scholarly work deeply based on medieval sources but with an appeal for more ‘factual history’. This article presents the note’s first diplomatic edition with an English translation.",
		"collection-number": "6",
		"collection-title": "Africana Ambrosiana",
		"container-title": "Envisioning and Representing Africa. Immaginare e rappresentare l'Africa",
		"ISBN": "979-12-5692-137-9",
		"language": "English",
		"page": "133–145",
		"publisher": "Biblioteca Ambrosiana, Centro Ambrosiano",
		"publisher-place": "Milano",
		"title": "On the Invention of an Autobiography for an alleged royal Chronicler at the Ethiopian Court: Analysis, Edition and Translation of the 'Autobiography' of Krəstos Ḫarayo as attested in MS  EMML 1614",
		"author": [
			{
				"family": "Valieva",
				"given": "Nafisa"
			}
		],
		"editor": [
