	{
		"id": "http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/MRAP5SNB",
		"type": "chapter",
		"abstract": "Abstract\n            The meaning of the term ‘Apocrypha’ is ambiguous in both early Christian and modern usage. This article covers the apocryphal and deutero-canonical books included in the NRSV, and the term ‘Apocrypha’ is used with this specific meaning. Reference is also made to the Book of Enoch (1 Enoch) because it, like the Book of Jubilees, is regarded as canonical by the Ethiopian Church. The writings of the Apocrypha have in common the fact that although none belong in the Hebrew Bible, they all, with the exception of 2 Esdras, are included in manuscripts of the Greek Bible.",
		"container-title": "The Oxford Handbook of Biblical Studies",
		"DOI": "10.1093/oxfordhb/9780199237777.003.0010",
		"ISBN": "978-0-19-923777-7",
