	{
		"id": "http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/3BZGZ77V",
		"type": "article-journal",
		"abstract": "The heresiographical literature best known to Islamicists is largely the product of Muʿtazilite and Ashʿarite scholars. This paper is a preliminary study of an alternative heresiographical tradition, produced and transmitted originally in eastern Ḥanafite circles. It includes an identification of some of the basic texts now available, a discussion of their distinctive literary features, and two brief case studies which directly compare eastern and standard material. It is suggested that in some cases the eastern literature offers a way behind the classical Muʿtazilite-Ashʿarite tradition.",
		"container-title": "Journal of the American Oriental Society",
		"DOI": "10.2307/606164",
